From d6efa15c2780227edcb13e01e04f842c9e9825a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 13:44:03 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(desktop): sessions waiting on a code review stripe red,
 or grey while only others were asked <24h [daveey]

Backend stamps review_wait on session rows whose latest assistant reply links
an open GitHub PR with reviewDecision=REVIEW_REQUIRED (viewer-authored or
asking the viewer): 'stuck' when the review is on the viewer, nobody is
requested, or others were asked over 24h ago; 'parked' when only others were
requested in the last 24h. gh lookups run on a background thread, cached 5 min.
The sidebar/tab stripe maps stuck -> red and parked -> grey (like Cmd-B);
both beat a running watcher and done, never a working turn.
